   "detail": {
    "seconds": 7.0,
    "decision": "proceed",
    "plan": "Question: Compare shop-wide performance during the Diwali 2026 and Diwali 2025 sale-event windows.\nMetrics: Orders = COUNT(DISTINCT sales.order_id), Realized revenue = SUM(CASE WHEN delivered_at IS NOT NULL THEN net_amount - COALESCE(refund_amount, 0) ELSE 0 END), Net sales = SUM(CASE WHEN cancelled_at IS NULL THEN net_amount ELSE 0 END), Orders, realized revenue and net sales per day = each event total divided by its inclusive event-window length\nBreakdowns: sale event\nFilters: sale_events.name IN ('Diwali 2025', 'Diwali 2026'); sales.line_type = 'Sale'\nTime window: 2025-01-01 to 2026-11-14 inclusive; within this range, use each event's start_date through end_date inclusive. Exact event dates are not supplied and must be retrieved from sale_events.\nComparison: Diwali 2026 versus Diwali 2025, including per-day figures for differing event lengths.\nExpected result: One row per event, with event name, start and end dates, event days, orders, realized revenue, net sales and their per-day averages.\nAssumptions: Include all shop sales placed during each event window, not just lines linked to its event_id; events may overlap.; Recent realized revenue may be incomplete because delivery and returns are still pending."
   },
   "t": 7.15
  },
  {
   "type": "step",
   "step": "write_sql",
   "status": "started",
   "detail": {},
   "t": 7.15
  },
  {
   "type": "step",
   "step": "write_sql",
   "status": "done",
   "detail": {
    "seconds": 9.67,
    "attempt": 1,
    "sql": "WITH event_totals AS (\n  SELECT e.event_id, e.name AS event_name, e.start_date, e.end_date,\n         date_diff('day', CAST(e.start_date AS DATE), CAST(e.end_date AS DATE)) + 1 AS event_days,\n         COUNT(DISTINCT s.order_id) AS orders,\n         COALESCE(SUM(CASE WHEN s.delivered_at IS NOT NULL THEN s.net_amount - COALESCE(s.refund_amount, 0) ELSE 0 END), 0) AS realized_revenue,\n         COALESCE(SUM(CASE WHEN s.cancelled_at IS NULL THEN s.net_amount ELSE 0 END), 0) AS net_sales\n  FROM sale_events e\n  LEFT JOIN sales s ON s.placed_at >= CAST(CAST(e.start_date AS DATE) AS TIMESTAMP)\n    AND s.placed_at < CAST(CAST(e.end_date AS DATE) AS TIMESTAMP) + INTERVAL 1 DAY\n    AND s.placed_at >= TIMESTAMP '2025-01-01'\n    AND s.placed_at < TIMESTAMP '2026-11-15'\n    AND s.line_type = 'Sale'\n  WHERE e.name IN ('Diwali 2025', 'Diwali 2026')\n  GROUP BY e.event_id, e.name, e.start_date, e.end_date\n)\nSELECT event_name, start_date, end_date, event_days, orders, realized_revenue, net_sales,\n       orders * 1.0 / NULLIF(event_days, 0) AS orders_per_day,\n       realized_revenue / NULLIF(event_days, 0) AS realized_revenue_per_day,\n       net_sales / NULLIF(event_days, 0) AS net_sales_per_day\nFROM event_totals\nORDER BY start_date",
    "explanation": "Compares shop-wide sales placed in each event window, including per-day figures based on the full inclusive event length. Recent realized revenue may be incomplete while deliveries and returns are pending."
   },
